<task id="001" project="spaarkeai-compose-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>Add `Docxodus` 7.1.0 (SkiaSharp excluded) + bump OpenXml 3.4.1→3.5.1; publish-size + CVE baseline</title>
    <phase>0 Foundations</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W0</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,docx,azure</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5-1 day</estimated-effort>
    <assigned>unassigned</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add the `Docxodus` 7.1.0 NuGet package (MIT, .NET 10 — the `WmlComparer` redline engine adopted
    for E1) to `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj`, with its transitive **SkiaSharp
    assets EXCLUDED** via `&lt;ExcludeAssets&gt;runtime;native&lt;/ExcludeAssets&gt;` on the SkiaSharp reference
    (Spike S3 proved `WmlComparer` runs with SkiaSharp fully removed — the 11.6 MB native is not
    needed for the diff). Bump `DocumentFormat.OpenXml` 3.4.1 → 3.5.1 in the same csproj. Then measure
    BFF publish size (`dotnet publish -c Release … -o deploy/api-publish/`) — report absolute
    compressed size + delta vs the ~49.63 MB baseline — and confirm `dotnet list package --vulnerable
    --include-transitive` is clean for the two additions. This is the packaging foundation for the
    entire E1/E2 fidelity core (tasks 010, 020, 021, 022); it lands the dependency and proves the
    budget/CVE gates BEFORE any consuming code is written. No consuming code in this task.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 build/packaging engineer fluent in MSBuild `PackageReference` metadata
    (`ExcludeAssets`, transitive-dependency pruning), the Microsoft Open XML SDK 3.x
    (`DocumentFormat.OpenXml`), NuGet vulnerability scanning, and the Spaarke BFF publish-size
    discipline (ADR-029 / CLAUDE.md §10). Comfortable reasoning about SkiaSharp native-asset exclusion
    on a transitive reference.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj` references `Docxodus` 7.1.0 with SkiaSharp runtime/native assets excluded,
    and `DocumentFormat.OpenXml` bumped 3.4.1 → 3.5.1. The BFF builds green; the published output
    stays ≤ 60 MB compressed with the net Docxodus add ≈ 2.44 MB uncompressed (~1 MB compressed) per
    S3; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` reports no new HIGH CVE from either
    addition. Publish-size absolute + delta vs the ~49.63 MB baseline is recorded in the task notes /
    PR description, stating the PDB convention. No Docxodus code path is invoked yet.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      E1 (retained-original delta save, design §4) adopts `Docxodus` `WmlComparer` (MIT, .NET 10,
      a maintained fork of Microsoft's archived Open-Xml-PowerTools) to synthesize minimal
      `w:ins`/`w:del` redline markup between the retained original and the spliced-edited document —
      "prior art we adopt, not code we write" (design §4.2). Spike S1/S1b confirmed adoption; Spike S3
      resolved publish-size: Docxodus managed = 2.44 MB, and its `SkiaSharp` transitive dependency
      ships an 11.6 MB win-x64 native (`libSkiaSharp.dll`) that `WmlComparer` does NOT need for the
      diff, so SkiaSharp assets are excluded (design §12.3). This is the FIRST task to add the NuGet;
      it establishes the packaging + budget + CVE baseline before tasks 020/021/022 consume it. Open
      XML SDK is already a BFF dependency (design §9) — this is only a minor 3.4.1 → 3.5.1 bump.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj — add `Docxodus` 7.1.0 (SkiaSharp assets excluded via `&lt;ExcludeAssets&gt;runtime;native&lt;/ExcludeAssets&gt;`); bump `DocumentFormat.OpenXml` 3.4.1 → 3.5.1 (design §38 Affected Areas, §12.3)</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/notes/spikes/S1-docxodus-wmlcomparer-2026-07-16.md — S1 WmlComparer PASS (engine + paraId preservation)</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/notes/spikes/S1b-S2-S4-S5-2026-07-16.md — S1b/S3 evidence (SkiaSharp-excluded run; 2.44 MB net add)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §12.3 (Docxodus publish-size + SkiaSharp exclusion), §4.2 (WmlComparer adoption), §14 (S1/S3 spikes)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">No task dependency. Consumes the S1/S1b/S3 spike results (already passed, in notes/spikes/). Blocks tasks 003, 010, 020, 021, 022 (the fidelity core that consumes Docxodus).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 / §10 BFF hygiene / ADR-029">Measure BFF publish size after adding Docxodus + bumping OpenXml: `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report absolute compressed size + delta vs the ~49.63 MB baseline. Docxodus net add ≈ 2.44 MB (managed, SkiaSharp excluded); ≥ +5 MB single-task delta → justify; ≥ 55 MB cumulative → architecture review; ≥ 60 MB → HARD STOP. State the PDB convention when reporting.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 / design §12.3 (S3)">MUST exclude SkiaSharp assets when adding Docxodus — `&lt;ExcludeAssets&gt;runtime;native&lt;/ExcludeAssets&gt;` on the transitive SkiaSharp ref (or a targeted `runtimes/` exclusion). Without exclusion the 11.6 MB native re-inflates the publish.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 / design §13 (BINDING packaging note)">MUST NOT invoke any Docxodus code path that touches `HtmlToWml` or `FormattingAssembler` — those re-pull SkiaSharp. The R3 splice uses `WmlComparer` only. (This task adds no consuming code; the constraint binds all downstream consumers and is stated here as the packaging invariant.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-02 / ADR-029">`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` MUST be clean for the Docxodus + OpenXml 3.5.1 additions — no NEW HIGH CVE. A pre-existing transitive HIGH not introduced by this change is not a regression but MUST be called out.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03 / project">Only permissive licenses — Docxodus is MIT, Open XML SDK is MIT. No AGPL/copyleft. Zero commercial license fees.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">State the Placement Justification (all R3 server work in `Sprk.Bff.Api`; this is a csproj-only packaging change reusing the existing BFF project) in the PR description, citing bff-extensions.md decision criteria.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>NuGet transitive-asset exclusion (SkiaSharp); Open XML SDK version bump; BFF publish-size + CVE discipline</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="PackageReference asset exclusion" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj">
        Add `&lt;PackageReference Include="Docxodus" Version="7.1.0" /&gt;`; exclude SkiaSharp via a sibling `&lt;PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp" ... &gt;&lt;ExcludeAssets&gt;runtime;native&lt;/ExcludeAssets&gt;&lt;/PackageReference&gt;` (or `runtimes/` prune). Bump the existing `DocumentFormat.OpenXml` entry 3.4.1 → 3.5.1 in place.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + spike review">Declare the rigor level (FULL). Read the S1/S1b/S3 spike notes to confirm the SkiaSharp-excluded WmlComparer run and the 2.44 MB net-add figure. Load bff-extensions.md + ADR-029 before editing the csproj. Capture the CURRENT publish-size baseline first (pre-change) so the delta is exact.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Add Docxodus + exclude SkiaSharp">Add `Docxodus` 7.1.0 to `Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj`. Add the SkiaSharp asset exclusion (`&lt;ExcludeAssets&gt;runtime;native&lt;/ExcludeAssets&gt;` on the transitive ref, or targeted `runtimes/` exclusion). Restore and confirm the SkiaSharp native is NOT in the output.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Bump Open XML SDK">Bump `DocumentFormat.OpenXml` 3.4.1 → 3.5.1 in the same csproj. Restore.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Build">`dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` — confirm green (0 errors) with the new dependency graph.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Publish-size measurement">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; measure the compressed output; verify no `libSkiaSharp` native landed; record absolute size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline. State the PDB convention (incl/excl PDBs).</step>
    <step order="5" name="CVE scan">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; confirm no NEW HIGH CVE from Docxodus or OpenXml 3.5.1; call out any pre-existing transitive HIGH as not-introduced-here.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Report + index">Record the Placement Justification, publish-size absolute + delta, and CVE result in task notes / PR description. Update TASK-INDEX status.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj (Docxodus 7.1.0 with SkiaSharp excluded; OpenXml 3.4.1→3.5.1)</output>
    <output type="report">Publish-size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (PDB convention stated); CVE scan result; SkiaSharp-native-absent confirmation; Placement Justification</output>
  </outputs>

  <justification>
    <existing>No in-repo component performs paragraph-level OOXML redline synthesis (minimal `w:ins`/`w:del` diff between two DOCX). `DocxAnnotationWriter` (R2) writes only the AI-redline subset from a known annotation list; it does not diff two documents. No overlap — verified against `Services/Compose/` (design §10 reuse map lists WmlComparer as the sole net-new engine).</existing>
    <extension>The closest existing service (`DocxAnnotationWriter`) cannot be extended into a general two-document comparer without reimplementing the WmlComparer algorithm (Move Detection + Format-Change Detection). Adopting the maintained MIT engine is strictly cheaper and lower-risk than hand-writing paragraph add/remove/reorder diff (design §4.2, §11 Path C).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without Docxodus the E1 delta save (task 020/021/022) cannot synthesize minimal tracked-change markup from direct typing — dirty saves stay lossy (the exact FR-01 defect R3 exists to fix). Concrete failing contract: FR-03 acceptance "3 edited paragraphs → minimal ins/del" is unachievable.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">`Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj` references `Docxodus` 7.1.0 with SkiaSharp `runtime;native` assets excluded; the published output contains NO `libSkiaSharp` native (verified in `deploy/api-publish/`) — per NFR-01 / S3.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`DocumentFormat.OpenXml` is bumped 3.4.1 → 3.5.1; the BFF builds green (0 errors).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size is reported absolute + delta vs the ~49.63 MB baseline, ≤ 60 MB compressed, net Docxodus add ≈ 2.44 MB uncompressed (~1 MB compressed); the PDB convention is stated — per NFR-01.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` shows no NEW HIGH CVE from the Docxodus or OpenXml 3.5.1 additions — per NFR-02.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Only MIT-licensed dependencies are added (Docxodus MIT, OpenXml MIT); no AGPL/copyleft — per NFR-03.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No Docxodus `HtmlToWml`/`FormattingAssembler` code path is referenced (no consuming code in this task); the packaging invariant is documented for downstream consumers — per NFR-01 / design §13.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Placement Justification is stated in the PR description citing bff-extensions.md.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>

  <notes>
    **Completed 2026-07-16** (Opus 4.8 @ high, FULL rigor).

    **§6.5 Path-C deviation — Docxodus 7.1.0 → 6.4.0**: 7.x targets net10.0 ONLY (NU1202 on the
    net8.0 BFF). 6.4.0 is the highest release on the net8.0 line of the same MIT fork ("upgraded to
    .NET 8.0"), same WmlComparer engine, and pulls DocumentFormat.OpenXml 3.5.1 transitively (matches
    the task's bump target). The S1/S1b/S3 spikes validated engine behavior on a net10 scratchpad
    harness and did NOT catch net8 consumability — spike-coverage gap noted for the hardening gate
    (task 003). DOC-RECONCILE FOLLOW-UP: design §12.3 + tasks 010/020/021/022 prose still say "7.1.0";
    update to "6.4.0 (net8.0 line)".

    **SkiaSharp exclusion (linux-x64 RID)**: 6.4.0 delivers the native via
    SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux.NoDependencies 3.119.4 (not the win-x64 native). Excluded
    runtime;native on BOTH `SkiaSharp` 3.119.4 and `SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux.NoDependencies`
    3.119.4. Verified: 0 SkiaSharp managed dll, 0 native, no runtimes/ dir in publish.

    **Measurements** (deploy/api-publish, compressed incl. PDBs via Compress-Archive Optimal):
    - Fresh pre-change baseline: 46.66 MB compressed / 140.89 MB uncompressed / 240 files
      (below the documented 49.63 MB baseline because this worktree is rebased past ai-redesign-r1's
      ~11.8k-line deletion sweep).
    - Post-change: 47.26 MB compressed / 142.72 MB uncompressed / 241 files.
    - Delta: +0.60 MB compressed (+1.83 MB uncompressed = Docxodus.dll 1.82 MB). Under +5 MB
      escalation threshold; far under 55/60 MB ceilings.
    - CVE: no NEW HIGH from Docxodus/OpenXml. Pre-existing HIGH = Microsoft.Kiota.Abstractions
      1.21.2 (GHSA-7j59-v9qr-6fq9), Graph SDK chain, accepted risk per ADR-029 — NOT introduced here.

    **Placement Justification (§10)**: csproj-only packaging change reusing the existing Sprk.Bff.Api
    project; no new project/service. All R3 server work lives in the BFF (Services/Compose). Per
    bff-extensions.md decision criteria the addition belongs in-BFF (consumed only by the BFF Compose
    save path). No new endpoint, DI registration, or AI-internal injection.

    **Quality gate (Step 9.5, inline)**: ADR-029 four MUST rules intact (linux-x64 framework-dependent,
    sourcemap exclusion, transitive-CVE overrides, ≤60 MB); no new HIGH CVE. Full /code-review +
    /adr-check skills not spawned (single declarative csproj); available on request.

    **Files modified**: src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj (Docxodus 6.4.0 +
    SkiaSharp×2 exclusion + OpenXml 3.4.1→3.5.1).
  </notes>
</task>
